{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Lesson 10: Thermodynamics II: Reversibility and the Relative Energy Scale\n",
    "The Nernst equation tells us where a reaction sits. It does not tell us whether the reaction we get back on reversing the current is the one we started with, and it does not tell us what \"versus\" means on a voltage axis. Both matter enormously in practice.\n",
    "\n",
    "Today's topics:\n",
    "- Chemical and electrochemical reversibility\n",
    "- Working fluently on a relative voltage scale\n",
    "- Matching half-cell reactions to build a battery\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reference:**\n",
    "- Sections 1.1, 2.1 and 3.5 in *Electrochemical Methods: Fundamentals and Applications*, Allen J. Bard & Larry R. Faulkner.\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Configure Environment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
