  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 3. Reversibility\n",
    "\n",
    "Reversibility in electrochemical reactions is a nuanced subject that we will touch on throughout the course. There are two distinct types of reversibility:\n",
    "- **Chemical reversibility**: the reversal of current flow in the cell will change the direction of the reaction. \n",
    "- **Electrochemical reversibility**: A reaction is electrochemically reversible if the observed behavior *appears to be in equilibrium* as defined by the Nernst equation. Such reactions are referred to as being \"Nernstian\". This concept is non-trivial and will be addressed in more detail when we explore experimental techniques.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Example 1\n",
    "Consider the reaction cell below:"
   ]
  },
