   "source": [
    "cell2 = schemdraw.Drawing(inches_per_unit=0.75)\n",
    "cell2.add(elm.Line().right().length(2))\n",
    "cell2.add(elm.Line().up())\n",
    "cell2.add(elm.Line().left())\n",
    "cell2.add(elm.Line().left())\n",
    "cell2.add(elm.Line().down())\n",
    "cell2.add(elm.Line().right().length(2))\n",
    "cell2.add(elm.Gap().label('').down())\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# annotate diagram\n",
    "fig = cell2.draw()\n",
    "fig.plot([0, 0],[0.5, -0.5])\n",
    "fig.ax.annotate('Zn', (0.15,-0.5))\n",
    "fig.plot([-2, -2],[0.5, -0.5]) # cathode\n",
    "fig.ax.annotate('Pt', (-2.5,-0.5))\n",
    "fig.plot([-3, 1., 1., -3, -3],[-1.5, -1.5, 1.5, 1.5, -1.5], fill=(0,0,1,0.05)) # reaction cell\n",
    "fig.ax.annotate(r'$H_2O$, $H_2SO_4$', (-1.6,0), fontsize=10)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.fig.savefig('../Workspace/cell2.png')\n",
    "display(fig)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The possible reactions are:\n",
    "\n",
    "$2H^+ + 2e^- \\rightleftharpoons H_2$ ($E^0$ = 0 V)\n",
    "\n",
    "$ 1/2 O_2 + 2H^+ + 2e^- \\rightleftharpoons H_2O$ ($E^0$ = 1.23 V)\n",
    "\n",
    "$Zn^{2+} + 2e^- \\rightleftharpoons Zn_s $ ($E^0$ = -0.76 V)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Option 1: Zn anode and Pt cathode\n",
    "\n",
    "$2H^+ + 2e^-_{Pt} \\rightleftharpoons H_2$ \n",
    "\n",
    "$Zn \\rightleftharpoons Zn^{2+} + 2e^-_{Zn}$\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall reaction:\n",
    "\n",
    "$2H^+ + Zn \\rightleftharpoons H_2 + Zn^{2+}$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Option 2: Zn cathode and Pt anode\n",
    "\n",
    "$H_2O \\rightleftharpoons 1/2 O_2 + 2H^+ + 2e^-_{Pt}$\n",
    "\n",
    "$2H^+ + 2e^-_{Zn} \\rightleftharpoons H_2$ \n",
    "\n",
    "Overall reaction:\n",
    "\n",
    "$H_2O \\rightleftharpoons 1/2 O_2 + H_2$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div class=\"alert alert-block alert-success\">\n",
    "<b>Net outcome</b>: The identity of the reaction changes when the current reverses. The electrochemical cell is <b>chemically irreversible</b>.\n",
    "</div>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4. Working on the Relative Energy Scale\n",
    "\n",
    "Thinking in relative terms comes naturally to some, while others struggle. The interconversion between reference electrodes and combining of half-cell reactions require that you become fluent with the voltage system. Practice makes perfect: play with numbers and establish tricks for yourself to remember.\n",
    "\n",
    "Thinking horizontally can help:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1400x530 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# The reference electrode and redox couple tables live in echem.py so that every\n",
    "# lesson quotes the same numbers.  Colours come from the shared style sheet.\n",
    "reference_electrodes = echem.REFERENCE_ELECTRODES\n",
    "redox_couples = echem.REDOX_COUPLES\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(7, 2.65))\n",
    "ax = plt.subplot(111)\n",
    "ax.set_ylim(-1, 1)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(r'$E$ /V vs. NHE')\n",
    "ax.set_yticks([])\n",
    "ax.plot([-0.8, 1.3], [0]*2)\n",
    "\n",
    "bars = [0.1, -0.1]\n",
    "for i, (name, potential) in enumerate(list(reference_electrodes.items())\n",
    "                                      + list(redox_couples.items())):\n",
    "    label_height = 0.15 if name in reference_electrodes else -0.5\n",
    "    ax.plot([potential]*2, bars, label=name, color=echem.color(i))\n",
    "    ax.annotate(name, (potential - 0.015, label_height), fontsize=6,\n",
    "                rotation=90, color=echem.color(i))\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.savefig('../Workspace/potentialscale.png')"
   ]
